<title>USA: Massachusetts raises size of bond sale to $923 mln.</title>
<headline>Massachusetts raises size of bond sale to $923 mln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Massachusetts on Wednesday said that it increased the size of its bond sale to almost $923 million due to favorable market conditions.</p>
<p>Ken Olshansky, deputy treasurer, said that the offering, which initially was planned for around $700 million, was divided between about $722.6 million of refunding bonds and another $200 million of new money bonds.</p>
